+Several source details affect the arithmetic. The WhisperTRT README labels memory as MB, while its profiler computes MiB and samples an RSS difference rather than a peak. Its `base.en` ratio is 439/666 = 65.9% of the original path's reported memory; the report uses the actual values rather than treating the promotional “about 60%” as precise. The independent speech paper's printed WER formula contains an apparent insertion-term typo; the interpretation here uses the conventional `(substitutions + deletions + insertions) / reference words`. Table 3 reports 328 seconds of clean audio, which supports aggregate real-time-factor arithmetic from its processing times. The code was unavailable at access time. These clip-based totals do not establish sustained continuous-stream latency or whole-device wall energy.
 
 The accompanying `deployment_calculations.py` and `calculation-results.json` contain the executed memory, phase-time, clip-RTF, power-duty, transfer and economic arithmetic. They run no model inference and make no claim to validate a device.
 
